d 'ADDLOGO': module to stamp a logo onto a Stata graph
d
d  Stata cannot place a raster image inside the plot region, so
d addlogo exports the current (or named) graph and composites a
d logo onto it, sized relative to the graph width so it looks the
d same at any export resolution. It stamps the current graph, a
d named graph, a saved .gph, or an already-exported image; nine
d positions, opacity, and PNG / TIF / JPG / PDF output. The
d compositing is done by ImageMagick (the "magick" CLI) or by a
d Python + Pillow helper -- whichever is present (engine(auto)).
d addlogo [using image] , logo(file) saving(file) [position()
d scale() ...] ImageMagick (brew install imagemagick), or Python 3
d + Pillow (pip install Pillow). 
d
d KW: graph; logo; image; branding; watermark; export
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f addlogo.ado
f addlogo.sthlp
f addlogo_helper.py
